# Per-machine build/signing config for Deskflow. This file is canonical.
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) on each seat and fill in the values for THAT box:
#
#   cp env.example .env
#
# Read by .vscode/tasks.json, scripts/build-windows.ps1, scripts/install-macos.sh
# and the fleet deploy scripts. Values here are per-seat identifiers and paths,
# plus -- on the Macs only -- the passwords the unattended deploy needs.
#
# Password rules (scripts/fleet-deploy.sh, scripts/fleet-deploy-macos.sh and
# tools/fleet-doctor all enforce them):
#   * the moment any *PASSWORD* value in this file is non-empty the file MUST
#     be mode 600:  chmod 600 .env
#   * .env must never be tracked by git (it is gitignored; fleet-doctor fails
#     if `git ls-files --error-unmatch .env` succeeds)
#   * passwords never go in scripts/fleet.env (copied to every seat;
#     fleet-doctor fails on any *PASSWORD* key in scripts/fleet.env*)
#   * Windows (tiny11) needs NO password anywhere: signtool and the service
#     manager run in the High-Integrity SSH session; the controller transports
#     nothing to a Windows seat and fleet-doctor fails on a password there

# ===== macOS (code signing) =====
# Your Apple Development certificate's SHA-1 HASH (not its name -- the hash is
# unambiguous even if two same-named certs are in the keychain). Required on
# both Macs: strict signing (FLEET_STRICT_SIGNING) refuses to build without it.
# Find it with:  security find-identity -v -p codesigning
DESKFLOW_CODESIGN_ID=

# ===== macOS (unattended fleet deploy) =====
# CONTROLLER side -- ONE line per macOS seat, ids as in scripts/fleet.env
# FLEET_HOSTS, lowercase: that seat's login password. scripts/fleet-deploy.sh
# reads these lines from the .env of the seat you run it on and hands each
# remote Mac its value on the SSH session's stdin (never argv, never
# fleet.env, never a log line; `bash -x` cannot echo it); the local seat gets
# it in-process. On the seat it becomes both DESKFLOW_KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD and
# DESKFLOW_SUDO_PASSWORD (below). A Mac without a line makes the controller
# refuse to start -- such a deploy would stall on a prompt -- unless
# --allow-prompts is given. One-time setup on the controller:
#   printf 'FLEET_SEAT_PASSWORD_hackintosh=…\n' >> ~/Desktop/deskflow/.env && chmod 600 ~/Desktop/deskflow/.env
# FLEET_SEAT_PASSWORD_hackintosh=
# FLEET_SEAT_PASSWORD_macbookpro=

# SEAT side (this box). Both optional; each defaults to the other and to this
# seat's own FLEET_SEAT_PASSWORD_<id> line above; a value set here beats one
# the controller transported. scripts/fleet-deploy-macos.sh captures both
# before any child process runs, so cmake, python3, codesign and the
# installers never inherit them.
#
# Login keychain password: the deploy runs `security unlock-keychain` +
# `set-key-partition-list` and proves codesign in the SSH session, so nothing
# is routed through the console GUI session (codesign over SSH otherwise
# fails with errSecInternalComponent). Mouser's scripts/build_and_install.py
# signs in that same session.
DESKFLOW_KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD=

# Login (sudo) password for the root steps: the LoginWindow bridge plist
# (scripts/install-login-bridge-macos.sh), the deskflow-prio LaunchDaemon +
# /private/var/db/deskflow (deskflow-ctl prio), root-owned retired files
# (deskflow-ctl retire), and chmod 600 + keystroke scrub of
# /var/log/deskflow-vhid-bridge.log -- all through `sudo -S` with the password
# on sudo's stdin. Unset (or rejected): those steps are printed for a human
# instead and the deploy still completes. The only steps left to a human
# either way: removing a BTM Login Item in System Settings, and a log-out for
# a new LoginWindow bridge plist to load.
DESKFLOW_SUDO_PASSWORD=

# Keychain that holds the identity above (default: the login keychain).
# DESKFLOW_KEYCHAIN=

# macOS: install destination (.app bundle path)
DESKFLOW_INSTALL_APP=/Applications/Deskflow.app

# ===== Windows (build dependencies + signing) =====
# Qt MSVC kit prefix (leave empty to auto-detect under C:\Qt)
DESKFLOW_QT_PATH=

# OpenSSL install root (e.g. C:\Program Files\OpenSSL-Win64)
OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR=

# Windows: install location (must be a full path, e.g. C:\Program Files\Deskflow -- not C:\Program)
DESKFLOW_INSTALL_DIR=

# Windows: SHA-1 thumbprint of the Authenticode signing cert (public identifier,
# not a secret). scripts/sign-windows.ps1 runs `signtool sign /sha1 <thumbprint>`.
# The same key is declared in scripts/fleet.env.example; either file may set it.
# Find it with:  Get-ChildItem Cert:\CurrentUser\My | Format-List Subject, Thumbprint
DESKFLOW_SIGN_THUMBPRINT=

# ===== Common =====
# Build output directory (relative to repo root)
DESKFLOW_BUILD_DIR=build

# Optional: override the settings directory used by scripts/sync-debug-settings-*.
# Default: ~/Library/Deskflow on macOS, %APPDATA%\Deskflow on Windows.
# DESKFLOW_SETTINGS_DIR=

# Login screen / UAC: configured in Deskflow GUI (Settings -> Advanced), not here.
# Requires the installed (Program Files) build + Deskflow Windows service + Start once while logged in.
